<title>USA: U.S. Defense Stockpile sells antimony, cadmium.</title>
<headline>U.S. Defense Stockpile sells antimony, cadmium.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Defense Stockpile Center announced Friday the sale of 132,000 pounds of antimony to Amalgamated Corp, of London for an approximate current market value of $120,000 after a tender.</p>
<p>The Stockpile also sold about 44,000 pounds of cadmium to American Iron and Metal of Montreal, Canada, for an approximate market value of $26,000.</p>
<p>The next tender for antimony and cadmium will be on April 8.</p>
<p>-New York Commodities Desk, +1-212-859-1640</p>
</text>
